1
00:00:56,015 --> 00:00:59,310
A WEEK BEFORE
THE LEADERSHIP AND MANAGEMENT AWARDS EVENT

2
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:02,104
Secretary Han, have you checked
Mr. Yoon's itinerary?

3
00:01:02,438 --> 00:01:04,190
We need to give it to him by tonight.

4
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:08,360
Draft the memory equipment investment plan
and send it to me by the end of this week.

5
00:01:10,696 --> 00:01:13,407
The two people
who asked to verify the retained earnings

6
00:01:13,491 --> 00:01:15,159
Mr. Yoon was investigating

7
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:17,661
are Executive Director Yoon Na-jung

8
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:19,914
and Chief Secretary Na Man-seok.

9
00:01:34,512 --> 00:01:38,349
After Secretary Han died,
the two of them came to see the chairman.

10
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:43,103
Okay. I need to hang up for now.

11
00:01:48,692 --> 00:01:50,861
Soon after Ms. Yoon left,

12
00:01:53,531 --> 00:01:55,449
Mr. Na went in to see the chairman.

13
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:01,872
And…

14
00:02:03,916 --> 00:02:05,793
You need to cover it up quickly, sir.

15
00:02:06,669 --> 00:02:08,504
They both told
the chairman the same thing.

16
00:02:08,587 --> 00:02:10,381
That he needs to cover up the case.

17
00:02:13,509 --> 00:02:15,177
On the surface, they were concerned

18
00:02:15,261 --> 00:02:17,513
about the company's image
and Mr. Yoon, the suspect…

19
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:19,181
But they had an ulterior motive.

20
00:02:20,975 --> 00:02:24,353
They feared the investigation
would expose their slush fund.

21
00:02:31,694 --> 00:02:32,653
What if

22
00:02:33,737 --> 00:02:35,698
word got out that we know something?

23
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:40,744
What do you think would happen?

24
00:02:42,454 --> 00:02:43,747
You want to leak our intel?

25
00:02:45,708 --> 00:02:48,377
The guilty will begin to panic.

26
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:51,422
They'll only take the bait
if the rumor sounds convincing.

27
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:53,048
We'll make it convincing.

28
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:54,633
We can also find out

29
00:02:55,134 --> 00:02:58,137
how far their connections
in the police go.

30
00:03:00,723 --> 00:03:03,559
The guilty will begin to panic.

31
00:03:03,642 --> 00:03:07,980
We can also find out how far
their connections in the police go.

32
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:10,024
He's going to use us?

33
00:03:13,444 --> 00:03:15,362
DAY OF LEADERSHIP
AND MANAGEMENT AWARDS EVENT

34
00:03:15,446 --> 00:03:16,447
Last time,

35
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:19,033
there was one thing I forgot to mention.

36
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:22,328
I gave Secretary Han a pen
with a recording function as a gift.

37
00:03:22,995 --> 00:03:24,121
I found that pen.

38
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:25,915
Are you submitting it as evidence?

39
00:03:25,998 --> 00:03:26,999
She doesn't have it.

40
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:30,669
Mr. Yoon asked for it,
so she had to give it to him.

41
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:34,840
What was on the recording?

42
00:03:35,424 --> 00:03:36,467
Did you hear it?

43
00:03:36,884 --> 00:03:37,885
No.

44
00:04:00,532 --> 00:04:02,451
It turns out
Lee Hye-jung had a recording pen

45
00:04:02,534 --> 00:04:04,745
in addition to the files.

46
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:08,999
She says she doesn't know
what was on the recording.

47
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,534
Wake up, Hye-jung.

48
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:45,285
Lee Hye-jung!

49
00:04:45,619 --> 00:04:48,163
Are you guys crazy? What were you doing?

50
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:49,790
-Hye-jung.
-Call the ambulance.

51
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:51,875
-Yes.
-Hye-jung.

52
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:53,836
Are you okay? Hye-jung.

53
00:04:55,462 --> 00:04:57,256
Are you okay?

54
00:04:59,508 --> 00:05:00,884
Are you all right, Ms. Lee?

55
00:05:05,597 --> 00:05:06,765
Was he inside your home?

56
00:05:07,933 --> 00:05:10,060
Did you see his face?

57
00:05:15,441 --> 00:05:16,692
Tattoos?

58
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:18,027
Show her the picture.

59
00:05:20,404 --> 00:05:21,780
Was it this tattoo?

60
00:05:23,866 --> 00:05:24,742
Yes.

61
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:26,785
-Go after him. He might be nearby.
-Yes, sir.

62
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:30,080
Who is he?

63
00:05:30,164 --> 00:05:32,458
He's the man who was seen
near Park Min-hwan's house.

64
00:05:53,604 --> 00:05:56,648
The 2026 Korea Leadership
and Management Awards

65
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:59,902
will begin with the opening address

66
00:05:59,985 --> 00:06:02,112
by Taekang Group's
Managing Director Yoon Yi-jun.

67
00:06:14,958 --> 00:06:17,503
-Hello?
-Hye-jung could've died if we'd been late.

68
00:06:18,587 --> 00:06:19,880
Secretary Lee…

69
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:21,882
What did you say?

70
00:06:21,965 --> 00:06:23,675
Everything is okay there, right?

71
00:06:26,428 --> 00:06:27,805
You're up now, sir.

72
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:30,766
Kang Jae-hee.

73
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:53,247
I have to catch him.

74
00:07:04,299 --> 00:07:05,801
Sir, we need to get up.

75
00:07:06,802 --> 00:07:07,886
Stop them!

76
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:09,346
Stop taking pictures!

77
00:07:10,222 --> 00:07:12,558
-You can't take pictures.
-Stop.

78
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,518
Put those cameras down!

79
00:07:14,935 --> 00:07:15,978
Put them away!

80
00:07:16,061 --> 00:07:17,729
You too! Stop taking pictures!

81
00:07:17,813 --> 00:07:19,731
-You're not allowed.
-Are you okay, sir?

82
00:07:20,816 --> 00:07:21,817
What about you?

83
00:07:24,528 --> 00:07:25,529
Stop them.

84
00:07:25,612 --> 00:07:27,656
Hey, I told you not to take pictures.

85
00:07:37,374 --> 00:07:42,045
I apologize for the inconvenience.
The opening address for the event

86
00:07:42,129 --> 00:07:45,424
has been canceled
due to unforeseen circumstances.

87
00:07:45,507 --> 00:07:48,093
I sincerely apologize
for the inconvenience once again.

88
00:07:48,177 --> 00:07:50,095
As listed on the official program,

89
00:07:50,179 --> 00:07:54,224
we'll begin introducing
the guests from around the world.

90
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,735
I'll do a security check.

91
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:12,492
Are you okay?

92
00:08:16,538 --> 00:08:19,166
Are you injured anywhere?

93
00:08:24,379 --> 00:08:25,964
That's a relief.

94
00:08:28,467 --> 00:08:29,760
Don't ever do that again.

95
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:32,304
Don't rush in without thinking about

96
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:34,264
what could happen.

97
00:08:36,642 --> 00:08:37,976
The same goes for you, sir.

98
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:40,145
Don't ever do that again.

99
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:45,525
I'm obligated to protect you,
but you're not.

100
00:08:47,611 --> 00:08:49,196
-Why?
-That's the reason

101
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:51,823
I am getting paid millions of won
every month.

102
00:08:51,907 --> 00:08:55,535
I am simply doing what I'm paid to do.

103
00:09:00,832 --> 00:09:02,668
You just did what you're paid to do?

104
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:05,963
Yes, so please,

105
00:09:06,755 --> 00:09:11,009
stop getting in the way
of me doing my job.

106
00:09:11,093 --> 00:09:12,135
That's enough.

107
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:21,603
I told you it would be risky.

108
00:09:22,521 --> 00:09:24,189
If you keep provoking them,

109
00:09:24,523 --> 00:09:26,942
you'll become their target
like you were today.

110
00:09:27,025 --> 00:09:28,110
You asked me

111
00:09:30,195 --> 00:09:32,072
why I hired you at a time like this.

112
00:09:34,658 --> 00:09:36,994
I needed someone to protect me.

113
00:09:37,411 --> 00:09:39,788
And I'm glad
that you're the one to do that job.

114
00:09:43,834 --> 00:09:44,835
But that's also why

115
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:49,089
I can't have you getting hurt.

116
00:09:51,258 --> 00:09:53,135
So don't say things you don't mean,

117
00:09:53,218 --> 00:09:55,304
like you're just doing
what you're paid to do.

118
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:06,815
Sir.

119
00:10:10,277 --> 00:10:11,903
Please don't act like that again

120
00:10:16,825 --> 00:10:18,493
for my sake.

121
00:10:44,102 --> 00:10:45,354
EPISODE 8

122
00:10:45,437 --> 00:10:47,022
Just for the time being, okay?

123
00:10:49,858 --> 00:10:51,026
Please come inside.

124
00:10:52,986 --> 00:10:54,237
Close the door.

125
00:10:57,074 --> 00:10:58,784
I can stay at a hotel.

126
00:10:59,409 --> 00:11:01,661
Think of my place as a hotel. It's nicer.

127
00:11:01,745 --> 00:11:03,705
-I'll go to my friend's, then.
-Come on.

128
00:11:04,247 --> 00:11:06,500
We both know you don't have any friends.

129
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,962
Do you want something warm? Tea or milk?

130
00:11:11,046 --> 00:11:13,465
I can buy medication
that will help you calm down.

131
00:11:13,548 --> 00:11:14,424
Forget it.

132
00:11:15,675 --> 00:11:17,344
You can give me a hug instead.

133
00:11:21,306 --> 00:11:22,140
Your loss.

134
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:34,778
I think you're the one
who needs something to calm yourself down.

135
00:11:35,695 --> 00:11:37,197
Your heart is racing.

136
00:11:38,365 --> 00:11:39,408
That's because

137
00:11:40,325 --> 00:11:41,701
you are…

138
00:11:43,912 --> 00:11:45,539
You were tearing up earlier.

139
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:48,125
You were about to burst into tears.

140
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:52,879
No one cried, okay?

141
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:56,675
I'll wear these.

142
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:00,220
Good.

143
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:03,974
Look at you finding them.
I left them out for you.

144
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:13,567
Mom.

145
00:12:14,359 --> 00:12:15,694
Mom.

146
00:12:15,777 --> 00:12:16,987
Mom, wake up.

147
00:12:19,531 --> 00:12:21,533
Secretary Han.

148
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:23,702
Mom.

149
00:12:24,327 --> 00:12:25,787
Mom, wake up.

150
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:28,123
Wake up.

151
00:12:38,049 --> 00:12:40,343
You're a cop
doing an undercover investigation.

152
00:12:41,553 --> 00:12:43,847
I trust you.
But don't let him control you.

153
00:12:45,682 --> 00:12:47,642
Everything went black,

154
00:12:48,518 --> 00:12:50,562
but all I could think about was you.

155
00:12:52,731 --> 00:12:53,982
So for now,

156
00:12:55,525 --> 00:12:57,110
let's just stay like this.

157
00:12:57,194 --> 00:12:58,778
Please don't act like that again

158
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,327
for my sake.

159
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:25,096
-Hey.
-Captain.

160
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:26,806
Did you look up the courier's number?

161
00:13:26,890 --> 00:13:28,308
Gosh, I'm tired.

162
00:13:28,892 --> 00:13:30,060
Did you?

163
00:13:32,646 --> 00:13:34,231
I confirmed the owner of the number.

164
00:13:34,314 --> 00:13:35,941
Please get it done by 10 a.m., sir.

165
00:13:45,867 --> 00:13:49,829
This little brat is gearing up
to cause trouble again.

166
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:59,005
DELIVERY AND COURIER SERVICE

167
00:13:59,089 --> 00:14:02,050
What is it? I'm a busy man.

168
00:14:02,384 --> 00:14:03,593
Someone is here for you.

169
00:14:06,137 --> 00:14:07,222
Detective!

170
00:14:13,728 --> 00:14:14,563
Hey.

171
00:14:16,273 --> 00:14:17,732
I told you, I don't remember.

172
00:14:17,816 --> 00:14:21,236
I deliver dozens of packages a day.
How am I supposed to remember everything?

173
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:23,280
Maybe this will help you remember.

174
00:14:29,703 --> 00:14:32,872
Nod your head if this is you.

175
00:14:33,373 --> 00:14:34,374
Look.

176
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:38,837
This lady…

177
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:41,673
She scares me.

178
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:42,924
But…

179
00:14:44,593 --> 00:14:48,179
she paid me 300,000 won
plus the delivery fee.

180
00:14:48,263 --> 00:14:50,640
So I just delivered the package,
nothing else.

181
00:14:50,724 --> 00:14:51,975
But why did you run?

182
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:55,145
If you do this job long enough,
you develop instincts.

183
00:14:55,228 --> 00:14:56,229
And you know what?

184
00:14:56,563 --> 00:14:58,565
The man who got it
was chasing me like crazy.

185
00:14:58,648 --> 00:15:00,150
What else was I supposed to do?

186
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:01,526
Like crazy?

187
00:15:01,610 --> 00:15:02,485
Yes.

188
00:15:06,281 --> 00:15:07,240
Did you see this?

189
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:08,825
Take a look.

190
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,745
-Did you see it?
-I did.

191
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:17,459
Have you looked into it?

192
00:15:17,542 --> 00:15:19,002
Was Yoon Na-jung behind it?

193
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:20,795
Did she have wild ginseng or something?

194
00:15:20,879 --> 00:15:23,006
Why is she so passionate about this?

195
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:27,469
The same MO was used to kill
Han Eun-young, like using his left hand.

196
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:30,972
He picked Lee Hye-jung's lock
despite us and security being there.

197
00:15:31,056 --> 00:15:33,224
Do you eat wild ginseng too?

198
00:15:33,308 --> 00:15:35,018
Let's just eat for now.

199
00:15:37,312 --> 00:15:38,647
I'll investigate Manager Choi.

200
00:15:38,730 --> 00:15:40,440
Detective Kang has a point.

201
00:15:40,523 --> 00:15:42,484
It wasn't just the courier.

202
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:44,694
Yoon Na-jung has
won over Yoon Yi-jun's people.

203
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:47,113
If we dig into Manager Choi,
things that happened--

204
00:15:47,197 --> 00:15:49,366
Do you think I don't know
what you already know?

205
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:52,285
They say to test the waters first.

206
00:15:52,786 --> 00:15:55,330
Let's eat our lunch first, okay?

207
00:15:55,997 --> 00:15:57,791
I'm worried about Detective Kang.

208
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,001
She might get hurt.

209
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:03,338
You should look into Manager Choi first.

210
00:16:04,089 --> 00:16:06,007
-Jae-hee can't take on more tasks.
-Okay.

211
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:09,678
Damn it.

212
00:16:11,012 --> 00:16:12,430
You pay for the food.

213
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:18,186
-He's from the article, right?
-He is.

214
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:20,146
I saw the video. Did you see it?

215
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:22,148
-I did.
-Mr. Yoon saved him.

216
00:16:23,566 --> 00:16:25,318
-I know.
-That's interesting.

217
00:16:25,735 --> 00:16:26,569
It's him.

218
00:16:27,237 --> 00:16:28,488
Look out!

219
00:16:34,452 --> 00:16:35,704
Here's your coffee.

220
00:16:35,787 --> 00:16:37,080
Thank you.

221
00:16:43,044 --> 00:16:44,838
KNIGHT IN SHINING ARMOR TO THE RESCUE

222
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:46,548
WHAT HAPPENED AT THE AWARDS CEREMONY?

223
00:16:50,969 --> 00:16:52,762
LEE SI-A

224
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:59,436
A billionaire heir
rescuing his personal secretary.

225
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:02,647
Yi-jun, you've become a superstar.

226
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:04,149
Get to the point.

227
00:17:05,525 --> 00:17:07,026
It's getting complicated, right?

228
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:08,611
Should I hang up?

229
00:17:08,695 --> 00:17:10,864
Life is a lottery, Yi-jun.

230
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:15,034
In life, 99 things out of 100
won't go your way.

231
00:17:15,118 --> 00:17:17,162
I'll hang up if you keep wasting my time.

232
00:17:17,245 --> 00:17:18,830
How long should I wait?

233
00:17:18,913 --> 00:17:22,250
You know I'm running out of patience.

234
00:17:28,465 --> 00:17:30,300
KNIGHT IN SHINING ARMOR TO THE RESCUE

235
00:17:31,092 --> 00:17:32,302
It's all over the Internet.

236
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:35,013
Even with the face blurred,
they recognize you right away.

237
00:17:35,096 --> 00:17:38,016
People are saying
it's like a scene from a bromance film.

238
00:17:38,767 --> 00:17:41,060
How does it feel
to become a star overnight?

239
00:17:41,644 --> 00:17:42,812
It's very uncomfortable

240
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:45,815
and unpleasant.

241
00:17:47,609 --> 00:17:48,693
Just stay.

242
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,863
Do you want to go on a blind date?

243
00:17:51,946 --> 00:17:54,282
Assistant Manager Kim
asked me to set you up with her.

244
00:17:55,658 --> 00:17:56,993
Is she pretty?

245
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,370
You're asking the right question.

246
00:17:59,454 --> 00:18:00,997
Who's your type?

247
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:04,626
Someone who isn't picky,
smiles a lot, and is innocent.

248
00:18:08,296 --> 00:18:11,466
Brace yourself. It'll soon be
Mr. Yoon's mother's death anniversary.

249
00:18:11,549 --> 00:18:14,677
Mr. Yoon goes into full hermit mode
ten days before and after.

250
00:18:15,261 --> 00:18:17,514
Didn't she pass away when he was young?

251
00:18:18,181 --> 00:18:21,142
-Is he still having a hard time?
-Yes, and probably until he dies.

252
00:18:22,227 --> 00:18:23,478
Even I would be traumatized.

253
00:18:33,404 --> 00:18:36,074
It's very uncomfortable and unpleasant.

254
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,415
Is she pretty?

255
00:18:54,968 --> 00:18:56,010
Is she pretty?

256
00:19:01,224 --> 00:19:02,183
Is she pretty?

257
00:19:04,435 --> 00:19:06,521
Is she pretty?

258
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:08,398
Is she pretty?

259
00:19:08,481 --> 00:19:09,691
So is she pretty?

260
00:19:09,774 --> 00:19:11,401
Is she pretty? Is she?

261
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:12,318
Is she? Really?

262
00:19:12,402 --> 00:19:13,987
So she's pretty? I bet she is.

263
00:19:20,535 --> 00:19:21,661
Secretary Jung.

264
00:19:21,744 --> 00:19:22,912
Hey, Ms. Kim.

265
00:19:23,413 --> 00:19:24,747
Kim So-mi, External Relations.

266
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:27,250
-Hello.
-Hello.

267
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:29,919
-Are you going for lunch?
-Yes.

268
00:19:30,378 --> 00:19:32,672
-Did you have lunch yet?
-Not yet.

269
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:36,175
If you don't mind, do you want to join me?

270
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:41,306
All right, you two,
go and enjoy your lunch together.

271
00:19:41,389 --> 00:19:42,432
You two look great.

272
00:19:43,016 --> 00:19:44,642
This is just perfect.

273
00:19:44,726 --> 00:19:47,270
What a good-looking pair.

274
00:19:48,354 --> 00:19:50,857
And here I am,
who couldn't sleep a wink because of you.

275
00:19:54,652 --> 00:19:55,653
I'm sorry.

276
00:19:55,737 --> 00:19:58,948
I told Secretary Jung,
but I guess he didn't tell you.

277
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:02,118
He did.
I heard you refused the blind date.

278
00:20:03,912 --> 00:20:06,289
But I still wanted to meet you.

279
00:20:06,998 --> 00:20:08,708
You never know when you meet someone.

280
00:20:12,003 --> 00:20:14,255
It'll be fun if you go out with me.

281
00:20:19,761 --> 00:20:22,221
-Enjoy.
-Yes, thank you.

282
00:20:36,694 --> 00:20:38,947
Has he been stressed about something?

283
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:40,615
So the rumors are true.

284
00:20:40,698 --> 00:20:43,451
He does eat a lot when he's stressed out.

285
00:20:44,035 --> 00:20:45,536
Why aren't you eating? It's good.

286
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:48,706
Toasting it in the oven
has made it nice and warm.

287
00:20:50,959 --> 00:20:53,127
Was there anything
to stress him out today?

288
00:20:54,545 --> 00:20:56,631
Where's Secretary Kang?
He's not having lunch?

289
00:20:57,507 --> 00:21:00,343
You know, Secretary Kang is quite popular.

290
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:02,637
There are plenty of women,
including Ms. Kim,

291
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:05,473
who are lining up to ask me
to introduce him to them.

292
00:21:05,556 --> 00:21:09,978
I see. Secretary Kang is on a blind date?

293
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:12,939
It's the calm before the storm,
but don't worry.

294
00:21:13,022 --> 00:21:15,400
That's why I came up
with a bigger picture.

295
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:19,529
With rumors about you and Secretary Kang
going around because of the video…

296
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:22,573
So Secretary Kang is
on a blind date with a woman?

297
00:21:22,657 --> 00:21:25,952
That would stop the rumor
about that damn bromance.

298
00:21:26,035 --> 00:21:28,287
You aren't stressed.
You're actually in a good mood.

299
00:21:29,372 --> 00:21:30,581
Gosh, look at you eat.

300
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:32,875
KNIGHT IN SHINING ARMOR TO THE RESCUE

301
00:21:32,959 --> 00:21:34,919
MR. YOON KEPT ASKING
IF THE SECRETARY WAS OKAY

302
00:21:35,420 --> 00:21:37,547
He can barely handle the sight of a belt.

303
00:21:38,339 --> 00:21:39,799
What are they going on about?

304
00:21:41,092 --> 00:21:43,261
-What?
-Stop giving him a hard time.

305
00:21:43,928 --> 00:21:46,556
He has a hard time
around this time of year even without you.

306
00:21:47,974 --> 00:21:50,351
Mi-jin, you don't think
I have a hard time?

307
00:21:50,435 --> 00:21:53,646
I've been through a harder time than him.
Why does everyone take his side?

308
00:21:54,188 --> 00:21:56,566
I take your side, don't I?

309
00:21:56,983 --> 00:21:59,944
Your brother has no one to take his side.

310
00:22:00,611 --> 00:22:02,238
So I should shut up and drink my tea?

311
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:03,489
Good girl.

312
00:22:06,743 --> 00:22:10,455
What did that secretary record?

313
00:22:12,290 --> 00:22:13,166
Do you know?

314
00:22:16,544 --> 00:22:18,046
It must be nice having no worries.

315
00:22:18,129 --> 00:22:21,090
Just stay as you are,
the peace-loving eldest daughter.

316
00:22:23,926 --> 00:22:25,928
You hate it, yet you keep watching.

317
00:22:26,888 --> 00:22:28,806
You're quite strange too.

318
00:22:28,890 --> 00:22:31,142
It's ridiculous
how everyone is praising him

319
00:22:31,225 --> 00:22:32,810
for saving his secretary.

320
00:22:32,894 --> 00:22:35,855
They're all going on about
how they look good together.

321
00:22:35,938 --> 00:22:37,899
I admit. They do look good together.

322
00:22:57,335 --> 00:22:58,252
Mi-jin.

323
00:23:00,171 --> 00:23:01,339
See you at Mom's memorial.

324
00:23:04,425 --> 00:23:05,551
Where are you going?

325
00:23:07,345 --> 00:23:09,180
Let's go see Yi-jun together.

326
00:23:10,807 --> 00:23:13,309
He won't come out anyway.
Just leave him be.

327
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:26,239
He wasn't mad at him
for coming to work 30 minutes late?

328
00:23:26,322 --> 00:23:28,032
And he also gave him his juice?

329
00:23:30,576 --> 00:23:32,745
-Thank you.
-I even thought

330
00:23:32,829 --> 00:23:34,872
I was seeing things.

331
00:23:37,542 --> 00:23:38,417
Drink up.

332
00:23:40,086 --> 00:23:42,380
I guess I was too slow to catch on.

333
00:23:44,549 --> 00:23:45,383
Here.

334
00:23:47,260 --> 00:23:48,344
Hold on.

335
00:23:50,513 --> 00:23:53,057
He wouldn't have hidden it at home,

336
00:23:53,141 --> 00:23:55,226
but look for something
like a recording pen.

337
00:23:55,309 --> 00:23:56,894
Yes, ma'am.

338
00:24:01,149 --> 00:24:02,358
Manager Choi.

339
00:24:03,317 --> 00:24:04,443
Yes?

340
00:24:07,488 --> 00:24:09,031
What you saw that day…

341
00:24:28,509 --> 00:24:32,889
I didn't tell anyone but you,
just as you instructed.

342
00:24:34,807 --> 00:24:36,017
If you want to live,

343
00:24:37,059 --> 00:24:38,394
you better keep quiet.

344
00:24:39,353 --> 00:24:40,188
Yes, ma'am.

345
00:24:56,120 --> 00:24:57,622
-My gosh.
-Ms. Choi Myeong-suk.

346
00:24:58,206 --> 00:24:59,207
I'm with the police.

347
00:25:01,125 --> 00:25:02,543
Let's have a chat.

348
00:25:07,715 --> 00:25:09,675
Sorry for coming unannounced.

349
00:25:10,551 --> 00:25:13,763
Did Dad say he'll disown me
if I skip again?

350
00:25:14,222 --> 00:25:15,723
If you know that, you should come.

351
00:25:19,894 --> 00:25:22,480
Yi-jun, Mom's memorial…

352
00:25:22,563 --> 00:25:25,483
It's cruel to do this to Mom,
who left because she hated that house.

353
00:25:27,485 --> 00:25:31,322
Dad doesn't like holding the memorial
somewhere else.

354
00:25:31,405 --> 00:25:32,531
I don't like this either.

355
00:25:33,115 --> 00:25:34,450
I don't even like going there.

356
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:36,661
What makes you think
I want to go that day?

357
00:25:36,744 --> 00:25:38,120
Please understand.

358
00:25:42,208 --> 00:25:45,461
Na-jung said something weird earlier.

359
00:25:46,003 --> 00:25:49,590
Something about your previous secretary
recording something.

360
00:25:51,509 --> 00:25:52,718
Is that what she said?

361
00:25:53,678 --> 00:25:54,929
Everything's okay, right?

362
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:58,641
I'm just worried
you'll be in trouble again.

363
00:26:01,769 --> 00:26:04,188
Stop worrying. You'll get more wrinkles.

364
00:26:17,493 --> 00:26:19,203
You protected me.

365
00:26:20,371 --> 00:26:22,957
He caught on so quickly that day,
but now that I want him

366
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:26,252
to know how I feel,
he's so slow to catch on.

367
00:26:29,672 --> 00:26:30,715
Is she pretty?

368
00:26:30,798 --> 00:26:32,383
"Is she pretty"?

369
00:26:34,385 --> 00:26:38,889
When it comes to looks,
I've never been outmatched.

370
00:26:40,766 --> 00:26:43,352
Fine, go on your blind dates.

371
00:26:43,936 --> 00:26:45,604
It's obvious what will happen.

372
00:26:51,527 --> 00:26:53,487
-I love you.
-I love you too.

373
00:26:55,156 --> 00:26:56,741
-Let's get married.
-I'd love to.

374
00:27:19,764 --> 00:27:21,724
So Secretary Kang went on a blind date.

375
00:27:22,808 --> 00:27:26,145
Is that why you are
in such a bad mood, honey?

376
00:27:26,604 --> 00:27:29,190
You already imagined
the two of them walking down the aisle.

377
00:27:29,273 --> 00:27:32,109
They went on a honeymoon too?
Gosh, you went too far.

378
00:27:35,988 --> 00:27:37,323
You wanted to keep him around.

379
00:27:38,366 --> 00:27:39,909
You should've seen it coming.

380
00:27:40,743 --> 00:27:43,079
You shouldn't have stepped in
at the event, either.

381
00:27:43,162 --> 00:27:45,623
How could I not
when it was obvious he'd get hurt?

382
00:27:46,791 --> 00:27:49,001
This isn't a storm in a teapot.

383
00:27:49,085 --> 00:27:50,753
If you can't hide your feelings,

384
00:27:51,587 --> 00:27:54,256
it's only a matter of time
before everyone finds out.

385
00:27:56,842 --> 00:27:58,677
CHAIRMAN'S OFFICE

386
00:28:00,012 --> 00:28:01,389
Here we go.

387
00:28:10,231 --> 00:28:12,650
We'll put a hold
on your lovesick jealousy.

388
00:28:14,235 --> 00:28:15,403
What are you going to do?

389
00:28:15,820 --> 00:28:17,154
Are you going to leak it?

390
00:28:27,289 --> 00:28:30,292
Taekang's heir and his male secretary.

391
00:28:30,793 --> 00:28:34,588
You can ignore the whispers
and pointing behind your back.

392
00:28:36,340 --> 00:28:37,675
But what about Secretary Kang?

393
00:28:39,760 --> 00:28:42,096
The chairman called you in today.

394
00:28:43,139 --> 00:28:44,265
But will he next time?

395
00:28:47,518 --> 00:28:48,853
I'm worried.

396
00:28:49,311 --> 00:28:51,605
I really am.

397
00:28:53,732 --> 00:28:54,900
Cheer up.

398
00:29:25,890 --> 00:29:27,892
TAEKANG GROUP
CHAIRMAN'S OFFICE

399
00:29:35,774 --> 00:29:37,151
He got called upstairs.

400
00:29:37,985 --> 00:29:38,944
Did he leave just now?

401
00:29:39,028 --> 00:29:41,363
What was in that box
that made you chase him?

402
00:29:42,072 --> 00:29:44,867
If you hadn't done that,
Mr. Yoon wouldn't have gone after you.

403
00:29:46,118 --> 00:29:48,162
I had to make sure as his secretary.

404
00:29:54,001 --> 00:29:57,254
Ms. Yoon's secretary team informed us
they'd be arriving in five minutes.

405
00:29:58,130 --> 00:30:00,174
They'll make an issue of you, too.

406
00:30:01,008 --> 00:30:02,259
Brace yourself.

407
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:08,933
So it worked out like this.

408
00:30:10,893 --> 00:30:12,686
My time has come.

409
00:30:17,316 --> 00:30:18,275
Hey.

410
00:30:22,571 --> 00:30:25,699
No wonder you were pretty for a boy.

411
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:31,580
Family really can be worse than strangers.

412
00:30:34,792 --> 00:30:36,710
I had no idea

413
00:30:38,087 --> 00:30:39,755
he had such a taste.

414
00:30:42,466 --> 00:30:43,676
Did you hit on him?

415
00:30:45,594 --> 00:30:47,179
Or did he hit on you?

416
00:30:47,888 --> 00:30:49,640
I'd rather not hear such vulgar talk.

417
00:30:49,723 --> 00:30:51,433
It doesn't matter who hit on whom.

418
00:30:51,517 --> 00:30:54,562
Thanks to that, he's screwed.

419
00:30:56,939 --> 00:31:00,192
The CM Team is working
to stop the video from spreading.

420
00:31:00,276 --> 00:31:04,029
But it's spreading faster than expected.
I'm not sure how much we can contain.

421
00:31:05,614 --> 00:31:07,866
Your reckless behavior

422
00:31:07,950 --> 00:31:09,994
is dragging this company through the mud.

423
00:31:11,579 --> 00:31:15,624
I'll find a way to restore
the image of the company.

424
00:31:22,506 --> 00:31:25,050
You take responsibility and clean it up.

425
00:31:28,804 --> 00:31:32,808
Have you not submitted
the weekly marketing report yet?

426
00:31:33,601 --> 00:31:36,770
The secretary's office is working on it.
We'll submit it soon.

427
00:31:36,854 --> 00:31:37,896
It's fine.

428
00:31:40,024 --> 00:31:42,067
I will do the briefing myself.

429
00:31:49,825 --> 00:31:52,870
Managing Director Yoon Yi-jun
has significant public recognition,

430
00:31:52,953 --> 00:31:54,580
so despite efforts to limit exposure,

431
00:31:54,663 --> 00:31:58,834
reactions across social media
and online communities have been intense.

432
00:31:58,917 --> 00:32:02,338
Sales of the Taekang Electronics
Series 7 phones and wearable devices

433
00:32:02,421 --> 00:32:06,842
that I dropped while trying to save
my secretary are up 12% from last week.

434
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:09,595
Taekang Motors CV90 that I arrived in
is also receiving

435
00:32:09,678 --> 00:32:11,221
a flood of reservation inquiries.

436
00:32:11,805 --> 00:32:14,516
The clothes and shoes I wore that day

437
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:17,186
have an exclusive presence
at Taekang Department Store.

438
00:32:17,269 --> 00:32:18,937
They have sold out,

439
00:32:19,688 --> 00:32:21,523
putting Taekang in a favorable position

440
00:32:21,607 --> 00:32:24,568
ahead of its upcoming contract renewal
with the Italian headquarters.

441
00:32:26,570 --> 00:32:29,365
The group spends tens of billions
every year promoting its image.

442
00:32:29,448 --> 00:32:30,699
That pointless awards event?

443
00:32:31,325 --> 00:32:34,119
This was far more profitable
than getting some awards.

444
00:32:38,499 --> 00:32:40,668
Right, I forgot to mention this.

445
00:32:41,543 --> 00:32:42,628
Apparently,

446
00:32:42,711 --> 00:32:45,839
the comments and photos posted
by the son who visited Fantasy Land

447
00:32:45,923 --> 00:32:48,717
on his mother's birthday
are making waves, too.

448
00:32:52,805 --> 00:32:56,266
This is why
people should be kind to others.

449
00:32:56,350 --> 00:32:58,394
What goes around comes around.

450
00:33:08,987 --> 00:33:10,322
I will be attending

451
00:33:11,907 --> 00:33:13,492
Mother's memorial.

452
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:17,079
I have something to tell you as well.

453
00:33:30,718 --> 00:33:32,428
Do you have evidence that he's screwed?

454
00:33:32,803 --> 00:33:34,680
Yes. Move.

455
00:33:37,349 --> 00:33:38,308
Because I do.

456
00:33:39,351 --> 00:33:40,227
I have evidence.

457
00:33:49,945 --> 00:33:51,029
How's this?

458
00:33:55,868 --> 00:33:57,536
Where's my face in here?

459
00:33:58,454 --> 00:34:00,289
I confirmed with the courier.

460
00:34:00,914 --> 00:34:03,417
Should I ask the police to investigate?

461
00:34:05,419 --> 00:34:09,006
Who knows? This may not have been
the first time you've done this.

462
00:34:10,215 --> 00:34:12,760
Technically, all this happened
because of that box.

463
00:34:13,343 --> 00:34:14,762
Are you still going to see him?

464
00:34:17,222 --> 00:34:18,640
You're pissing me off.

465
00:34:20,434 --> 00:34:24,396
Hey, even if I were the one who did it,

466
00:34:25,856 --> 00:34:28,275
what are you going to do about it?

467
00:34:30,110 --> 00:34:33,405
Thank you for
sending me that box, Na-jung.

468
00:34:56,386 --> 00:34:58,180
How did you get the CCTV footage?

469
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:01,350
Who told you to go digging
into something that dangerous?

470
00:35:01,433 --> 00:35:04,561
I couldn't let this one go,
so I asked the event organizers for help.

471
00:35:04,978 --> 00:35:07,314
I was going to tell you,
but things got complicated.

472
00:35:07,981 --> 00:35:10,984
She's going to use the ill rumor
going around to discredit you.

473
00:35:11,068 --> 00:35:13,612
I thought I had to stop it
before she went to the chairman.

474
00:35:14,404 --> 00:35:17,324
Ill rumor? Discredit me?

475
00:35:17,407 --> 00:35:20,285
The rumor won't help either of us.

476
00:35:20,911 --> 00:35:22,996
We need to set the record straight
while we can.

477
00:35:25,249 --> 00:35:27,751
I didn't go through all that

478
00:35:28,877 --> 00:35:31,129
just to become the star of some rumor.

479
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:37,928
You should get ready quickly.
Otherwise we may not make it in time.

480
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:55,529
You had a showdown
with Yoon Na-jung just now, right?

481
00:35:57,072 --> 00:35:59,575
Just how many informants do you have?

482
00:35:59,658 --> 00:36:02,369
Be honest. The rumor going around.

483
00:36:03,537 --> 00:36:04,913
Yoon Yi-jun likes you, right?

484
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:11,336
You're trying to close the investigation
like the world is about to end.

485
00:36:11,795 --> 00:36:13,005
So you know he likes you.

486
00:36:17,175 --> 00:36:19,094
He likes you even though you're a man?

487
00:36:20,012 --> 00:36:21,513
I know you're a girl, but…

488
00:36:21,597 --> 00:36:25,517
What I'm trying to say is that
he thinks you're a man.

489
00:36:25,601 --> 00:36:28,687
He won't get any closer.
He won't be able to.

490
00:36:29,730 --> 00:36:31,565
He has too much to lose.

491
00:36:31,648 --> 00:36:33,108
You can't, Jae-hee.

492
00:36:33,901 --> 00:36:36,403
You know you can't. It can never happen.

493
00:36:38,155 --> 00:36:39,031
Don't worry.

494
00:36:47,331 --> 00:36:49,583
Are you okay? That's a relief.

495
00:36:50,334 --> 00:36:51,960
Don't ever do that again.

496
00:36:52,711 --> 00:36:54,755
Don't rush in without thinking about

497
00:36:55,339 --> 00:36:56,632
what could happen.

498
00:36:58,592 --> 00:37:02,346
It would be easier to get over him
if he was just obnoxious.

499
00:37:04,932 --> 00:37:07,517
I didn't go through all that

500
00:37:08,602 --> 00:37:10,604
just to become the star of some rumor.

501
00:37:13,440 --> 00:37:16,944
Why are you getting swayed
over every word he says?

502
00:37:18,695 --> 00:37:19,988
Pull yourself together.

503
00:37:24,493 --> 00:37:28,580
Could it be that
Mr. Kang Jae-hee is seeing someone?

504
00:37:29,164 --> 00:37:32,751
Right? I heard he said
he wasn't going to go on a blind date.

505
00:37:32,834 --> 00:37:34,795
So why did he have lunch with you?

506
00:37:34,878 --> 00:37:36,296
I don't know.

507
00:37:36,380 --> 00:37:40,676
He apologized, but he was so polite
it actually annoyed me more.

508
00:37:40,759 --> 00:37:45,180
He said he ended up using me
without meaning to or whatever.

509
00:37:45,973 --> 00:37:47,015
I can't believe it.

510
00:37:52,521 --> 00:37:55,190
The cleaning king of the month.

511
00:37:55,273 --> 00:37:57,609
It's Bin!

512
00:37:58,527 --> 00:37:59,569
Congratulations.

513
00:38:00,445 --> 00:38:02,739
I'd like to thank Ms. Cho

514
00:38:02,823 --> 00:38:05,575
and all of my colleagues
for helping me win this award.

515
00:38:06,868 --> 00:38:08,954
I dare to promise

516
00:38:09,037 --> 00:38:11,915
that I, Jung Wan-bin,

517
00:38:12,958 --> 00:38:16,253
will win the battle against mold!

518
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:21,383
-Kill the mold!
-Kill the mold!

519
00:38:22,634 --> 00:38:23,969
Cheers.

520
00:38:25,387 --> 00:38:28,223
Eat up. It's on Bin today.

521
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:29,266
Eat up!

522
00:38:29,349 --> 00:38:30,600
-Thanks!
-Thanks!

523
00:38:30,684 --> 00:38:32,185
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

524
00:38:32,269 --> 00:38:33,770
Could I get more meat?

525
00:38:33,854 --> 00:38:36,857
-Hurry!
-More meat!

526
00:38:37,774 --> 00:38:40,277
-Let's eat up.
-Let's eat up.

527
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:42,112
-Only 100,000 won?
-Have some more meat.

528
00:38:42,195 --> 00:38:44,448
Bin, are you ready to take a picture?

529
00:38:45,824 --> 00:38:47,743
All right. Smile.

530
00:38:47,826 --> 00:38:48,869
Ma'am.

531
00:38:49,995 --> 00:38:51,663
I have portrait rights.

532
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:55,584
This isn't a face
you can just take a picture of.

533
00:38:56,084 --> 00:38:57,961
You may be one of the Bins,

534
00:38:58,336 --> 00:39:00,130
but there's a line you can't cross.

535
00:39:01,089 --> 00:39:04,885
We still need to keep our tradition.

536
00:39:04,968 --> 00:39:06,136
Here.

537
00:39:07,471 --> 00:39:08,430
What's this?

538
00:39:09,556 --> 00:39:12,100
It's the hall of fame
for the cleaning kings of Taekang.

539
00:39:15,228 --> 00:39:17,022
CLEANING KING OF THE MONTH
NOVEMBER

540
00:39:17,105 --> 00:39:18,065
Who's this?

541
00:39:18,148 --> 00:39:20,692
That's Mr. Kim.

542
00:39:21,485 --> 00:39:24,654
What floor did he work on?
I never saw him.

543
00:39:25,113 --> 00:39:26,615
Did he come here today?

544
00:39:26,698 --> 00:39:28,825
He quit shortly before you came.

545
00:39:28,909 --> 00:39:30,327
I see.

546
00:39:31,244 --> 00:39:33,205
Why is he all covered up?

547
00:39:33,288 --> 00:39:37,209
He had lots of tattoos on his body.

548
00:39:37,959 --> 00:39:39,294
Tattoos?

549
00:39:39,377 --> 00:39:41,004
I asked him in passing,

550
00:39:41,088 --> 00:39:44,132
and he said he didn't want anyone
to be surprised.

551
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:47,135
He's from Taekang Cultural Foundation.

552
00:39:47,219 --> 00:39:50,680
So I was a bit wary of him.
I was a bit biased.

553
00:39:50,764 --> 00:39:55,644
But he's very quiet and clean.

554
00:39:55,727 --> 00:39:58,939
It was a shame he quit
right when that thing happened,

555
00:39:59,022 --> 00:40:01,149
-so we couldn't say goodbye.
-That's right.

556
00:40:01,233 --> 00:40:02,234
That thing?

557
00:40:02,984 --> 00:40:04,486
-Well…
-You know.

558
00:40:05,278 --> 00:40:08,323
That thing with the secretary
from the TF team.

559
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:09,616
I see.

560
00:40:09,699 --> 00:40:11,535
Goodness me.

561
00:40:12,160 --> 00:40:14,579
-It's unfortunate.
-My glass is empty.

562
00:40:14,663 --> 00:40:16,206
Jeez.

563
00:40:20,669 --> 00:40:23,505
CLEANING KING OF THE MONTH
NOVEMBER

564
00:40:34,391 --> 00:40:37,477
Was it Ms. Kim?
Did you enjoy lunch with her?

565
00:40:39,104 --> 00:40:41,314
-Yes.
-Do you like her?

566
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:44,484
Are you going to date her?

567
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:47,779
I'm thinking about it.

568
00:42:31,299 --> 00:42:32,968
Do you miss your mother a lot?

569
00:42:37,639 --> 00:42:38,640
Never mind.

570
00:42:46,982 --> 00:42:47,941
You know,

571
00:42:52,153 --> 00:42:55,031
I'm reminded of that day
whenever I see a belt.

572
00:43:00,120 --> 00:43:01,538
People sometimes

573
00:43:02,914 --> 00:43:04,708
make decisions that affect their lives.

574
00:43:07,711 --> 00:43:09,129
My mother

575
00:43:10,547 --> 00:43:12,590
did something similar that day.

576
00:43:22,100 --> 00:43:23,226
Yoon Yi-jun.

577
00:43:23,727 --> 00:43:26,187
Mom said not to bother her
when she's drawing.

578
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:30,400
Mom always smiles when I surprise her.

579
00:43:31,109 --> 00:43:32,068
She likes it.

580
00:43:32,152 --> 00:43:33,361
NA-JUNG

581
00:43:43,288 --> 00:43:44,122
Mom!

582
00:43:46,124 --> 00:43:47,334
She had depression.

583
00:43:50,837 --> 00:43:54,299
If you think about it,
Na-jung was only 11 as well.

584
00:43:54,382 --> 00:43:55,759
Mr. Kim!

585
00:43:57,552 --> 00:43:59,846
If I hadn't opened that door,

586
00:44:01,723 --> 00:44:03,224
she wouldn't have seen the hell

587
00:44:03,308 --> 00:44:05,393
-that would be etched into her memory.
-Na-jung.

588
00:44:06,144 --> 00:44:07,228
It's okay.

589
00:44:07,896 --> 00:44:08,855
It's okay.

590
00:44:10,231 --> 00:44:12,859
She wouldn't have had the terrible thought

591
00:44:13,693 --> 00:44:16,196
she'd always be second to me
in our father's eyes.

592
00:44:18,531 --> 00:44:19,616
Ever since that day,

593
00:44:20,325 --> 00:44:22,744
hiding became a habit

594
00:44:23,912 --> 00:44:25,622
and silence became comfort.

595
00:44:26,956 --> 00:44:28,625
If I remained silent,

596
00:44:30,251 --> 00:44:32,504
nothing worse happened.

597
00:44:35,340 --> 00:44:37,342
That's also what you hoped as well.

598
00:44:37,425 --> 00:44:38,426
No.

599
00:44:40,678 --> 00:44:44,391
I only hoped for your safety,
not your silence.

600
00:44:50,563 --> 00:44:51,815
But weirdly,

601
00:44:54,484 --> 00:44:55,944
ever since I met you,

602
00:44:58,113 --> 00:45:00,281
it's getting harder to hide my feelings.

603
00:45:03,284 --> 00:45:04,953
The more I tried to hide it,

604
00:45:06,746 --> 00:45:08,081
the clearer it became.

605
00:45:11,251 --> 00:45:12,544
Perhaps that's why

606
00:45:14,087 --> 00:45:16,214
you already knew

607
00:45:19,634 --> 00:45:21,177
how I felt about you.

608
00:45:22,846 --> 00:45:24,180
Despite knowing everything,

609
00:45:26,474 --> 00:45:28,184
you didn't show it.

610
00:45:29,352 --> 00:45:30,270
It was cruel.

611
00:45:31,020 --> 00:45:32,480
Because it's my job to do so.

612
00:45:36,359 --> 00:45:37,569
What if…

613
00:45:40,405 --> 00:45:41,823
What if…

614
00:45:45,743 --> 00:45:47,579
If I call off my marriage with Si-a,

615
00:45:50,498 --> 00:45:51,708
are you going to like me?

616
00:45:54,043 --> 00:45:55,378
If I gave up my title

617
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:58,006
and became an ordinary man,

618
00:46:00,091 --> 00:46:01,468
would you like me then?

619
00:46:05,597 --> 00:46:08,391
You said you wanted to keep me around
for a long time.

620
00:46:10,560 --> 00:46:12,395
The same goes for me.

621
00:46:14,355 --> 00:46:15,815
This is just a what-if.

622
00:46:17,734 --> 00:46:18,818
What if that happens?

623
00:46:22,614 --> 00:46:24,741
What if one of us were a man

624
00:46:28,786 --> 00:46:30,246
and one of us were a woman?

625
00:46:34,792 --> 00:46:36,544
Would you have liked me?

626
00:46:38,922 --> 00:46:41,799
You said you dislike pointless what-ifs.

627
00:46:41,883 --> 00:46:45,428
Even if that were true,
what you said would never happen.

628
00:46:47,639 --> 00:46:49,474
I said I'd protect you.

629
00:46:50,767 --> 00:46:53,186
I never said I'd have feelings for you.

630
00:46:58,358 --> 00:46:59,651
But why does it feel like

631
00:47:02,820 --> 00:47:04,989
you have feelings for me too?

632
00:48:34,245 --> 00:48:35,371
I don't.

633
00:48:42,712 --> 00:48:43,755
Is your heart racing?

634
00:48:44,881 --> 00:48:46,007
Because mine's not.

635
00:48:49,135 --> 00:48:50,386
Is your heart fluttering?

636
00:48:50,470 --> 00:48:51,971
I don't feel anything.

637
00:48:52,430 --> 00:48:54,057
-What are--
-Do you want more proof?

638
00:48:59,437 --> 00:49:00,897
What do you think you're doing?

639
00:49:00,980 --> 00:49:02,607
Even if I kissed you 100 times,

640
00:49:03,483 --> 00:49:04,984
I wouldn't feel anything.

641
00:49:09,197 --> 00:49:10,698
I never would've felt this way

642
00:49:12,825 --> 00:49:15,370
if it weren't for you.

643
00:49:19,457 --> 00:49:22,418
I'll pretend I never heard this.

644
00:49:44,107 --> 00:49:44,941
I'll drive.

645
00:49:49,153 --> 00:49:50,697
If you keep acting like this,

646
00:49:51,739 --> 00:49:53,658
I have no choice but to quit.

647
00:49:54,158 --> 00:49:55,952
Is that the only threat you have?

648
00:49:56,494 --> 00:49:58,162
Do you think I'll stay back

649
00:49:58,246 --> 00:50:00,415
if you dismiss this
as one of my power trips?

650
00:50:00,498 --> 00:50:02,333
We don't have time for this.

651
00:50:02,667 --> 00:50:03,835
Didn't you say

652
00:50:05,002 --> 00:50:06,295
you'd find the slush fund?

653
00:50:07,922 --> 00:50:10,466
You even baited the police
with that recording pen.

654
00:50:10,550 --> 00:50:12,301
The chandelier, the milk, and the belt…

655
00:50:12,385 --> 00:50:14,053
You've been in danger multiple times.

656
00:50:15,138 --> 00:50:16,931
You need to face reality first

657
00:50:17,432 --> 00:50:19,100
when you're in danger.

658
00:50:19,183 --> 00:50:21,978
I wouldn't be standing here like a madman
if that were possible.

659
00:50:38,202 --> 00:50:39,245
You have become

660
00:50:41,914 --> 00:50:43,332
my reality.

661
00:50:45,877 --> 00:50:46,836
I…

662
00:50:49,464 --> 00:50:51,174
like you, Kang Jae-hee.

663
00:51:30,838 --> 00:51:31,756
Honey.

664
00:52:06,457 --> 00:52:07,708
What's wrong?

665
00:52:15,049 --> 00:52:16,467
Put the gear in neutral.

666
00:52:18,052 --> 00:52:19,470
I can't. It doesn't work.

667
00:52:24,016 --> 00:52:25,017
Mr. Yoon!

668
00:52:25,977 --> 00:52:27,019
Kang Jae-hee.

669
00:53:28,998 --> 00:53:31,250
You must be the real culprit.

670
00:53:32,710 --> 00:53:33,961
He's under my protection.

671
00:54:10,539 --> 00:54:12,208
I won't let you.

672
00:55:38,044 --> 00:55:39,378
Then, we'll now begin

673
00:55:40,087 --> 00:55:43,966
the memorial service
for Michaela Na Ji-hyun.

674
00:55:44,633 --> 00:55:48,220
In the name of the Father, and of the Son,
and of the Holy Spirit.

675
00:55:48,721 --> 00:55:49,597
Amen.

676
00:55:52,725 --> 00:55:54,560
Dear brothers and sisters,

677
00:55:54,977 --> 00:55:59,482
we have gathered here today
to remember Michaela Na Ji-hyun.

678
00:56:00,274 --> 00:56:02,693
As we commend
the departed Michaela Na Ji-hyun

679
00:56:02,777 --> 00:56:04,737
to the Lord's mercy,

680
00:56:05,321 --> 00:56:06,697
we begin this memorial service…

681
00:56:06,781 --> 00:56:07,740
RECORDING PEN ACQUIRED

682
00:56:07,823 --> 00:56:09,992
…with prayers for peace and comfort

683
00:56:10,618 --> 00:56:12,870
for all of us who remain.

684
00:56:20,503 --> 00:56:21,879
ROAD CLOSED

685
00:56:30,513 --> 00:56:32,807
Are you okay? Can you hear me?

686
00:56:34,683 --> 00:56:36,185
You need to take it easy.

687
00:56:36,644 --> 00:56:38,312
Are you in any pain?

688
00:56:39,146 --> 00:56:40,940
I had another person with me.

689
00:56:41,023 --> 00:56:43,067
-My secretary was in the car with me.
-Right.

690
00:56:43,150 --> 00:56:45,194
-We just finished treating the passenger.
-Yes.

691
00:56:47,071 --> 00:56:49,365
What happened? Is he hurt badly?

692
00:56:49,698 --> 00:56:52,868
Her injuries are serious,
so we're taking her to the nearest ER.

693
00:56:52,952 --> 00:56:54,787
Are you that woman's guardian?

694
00:56:57,998 --> 00:57:00,209
Did you say "woman"?

695
00:57:02,795 --> 00:57:03,879
Hold on!

696
00:57:24,692 --> 00:57:28,279
I bet quite a few people had
the wrong idea about you in the military.

697
00:57:29,321 --> 00:57:31,991
Has anyone told you that you are pretty?

698
00:57:34,827 --> 00:57:35,870
What are you doing?

699
00:57:36,537 --> 00:57:37,997
I'm your human hanger.

700
00:57:38,497 --> 00:57:42,334
Then why is the hanger turned around?

701
00:57:42,418 --> 00:57:43,794
Are you okay, Special Forces?

702
00:57:45,588 --> 00:57:47,381
Are you really being shy?

703
00:57:55,264 --> 00:57:58,893
Remember I said I would've fallen for you
if you were a girl?

704
00:58:00,186 --> 00:58:02,354
If I were a girl,

705
00:58:04,273 --> 00:58:05,566
would you have fallen for me?

706
00:58:06,775 --> 00:58:09,486
It was a pointless what-if.

707
00:58:55,908 --> 00:58:57,910
SPECIAL THANKS TO
CHOI HEE-JIN AND JUNG YOO-MIN

708
00:59:02,539 --> 00:59:03,791
Why did you…

709
00:59:03,874 --> 00:59:05,668
I want to be by your side as your man.

710
00:59:05,751 --> 00:59:06,585
I like…

711
00:59:06,669 --> 00:59:08,671
You got clingy and got rejected again?

712
00:59:09,505 --> 00:59:11,048
That didn't happen!

713
00:59:11,131 --> 00:59:12,466
You've lost it.

714
00:59:12,549 --> 00:59:15,261
Why didn't you tell me
you lost the recording pen on purpose?

715
00:59:15,344 --> 00:59:17,137
But as time went on, I regretted it.

716
00:59:17,763 --> 00:59:19,265
How could you give him your heart?

717
00:59:19,348 --> 00:59:22,101
You should've told me
when I confessed to you.

718
00:59:22,434 --> 00:59:23,936
I was a coward, Mr. Yoon.

719
00:59:24,395 --> 00:59:25,980
Attend it and announce the marriage.

720
00:59:26,355 --> 00:59:27,731
I love Jae-hee.

721
00:59:28,440 --> 00:59:30,109
So leave her alone.

722
00:59:30,484 --> 00:59:33,487
Translated by Leo Chung
